{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## RCA — confirmed root cause (Phase 1 complete)\n\n### Mechanism (proven at runtime, not read off the source)\n\n`_spawn_detached_drain` (`src/rebar/llm/enrich_drain.py:319-333`) calls `subprocess.Popen`\nwith `**_detach_kwargs()` (`start_new_session=True`) and **no `cwd=`**. A detached child\ntherefore inherits the parent's working directory and, by design, outlives the parent. This\nproject's workflow runs ordinary writes from `make worktree` worktrees that are removed\nafterwards, so the child routinely ends up holding a working directory that no longer exists.\nThe first `os.getcwd()` then raises `FileNotFoundError` — for the drain that is\n`_config_sources.repo_root`'s final `Path.cwd()` fallback, reached via\n`queue.claim` -> `_tracker` -> `config.tracker_dir` -> `load_config` -> `repo_root`. The child\ndies BEFORE appending its CLAIM event, so nothing is claimed and nothing drains.\n\n### Discriminating experiment\n\nTwo detached spawns, identical in every respect (`start_new_session=True`, `close_fds=True`,\nsame interpreter, same removal of the spawning directory mid-flight), differing ONLY in\nwhether an explicit `cwd=` was passed:\n\n- **no `cwd=`** -> `CHILD getcwd RAISED: FileNotFoundError [Errno 2] No such file or directory`\n- **explicit `cwd=`** -> `CHILD getcwd -> /private/tmp/spitbug`\n\nThat rules out the alternatives the shape of the traceback invites — `start_new_session`\nitself, `close_fds`, the PYTHONPATH bootstrap, and interpreter startup — since all are\npresent in the passing control. The sole discriminator is the explicit working directory.\n\nReproduced again as a unit test that drives the real `_spawn_detached_drain`, removes the\nspawning worktree with a real `rmtree`, and reads back what the real child resolved:\n`ERR FileNotFoundError` before the fix.\n\n### A detail that shapes the fix\n\nA `make worktree` worktree has its own real `.rebar/`, but its `.tickets-tracker` is a\n**symlink** to the canonical store (verified). So the tracker path a detach site is handed may\nitself be a path *through* the doomed worktree. Choosing `dirname(tracker)` unresolved would\npin the child to the very worktree it must not depend on — the durable answer is\n`dirname(realpath(tracker))`, the canonical store's repo root, with a walk up to the nearest\nexisting ancestor so the chosen directory is never itself dead.\n\n### The class: this is three sites, not one\n\nA sweep of every detached spawn in `src/rebar` found the identical omission at all three\nchildren that are designed to outlive their parent — none of them passes `cwd=`:\n\n| site | detached | explicit cwd | how it dies |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `llm/enrich_drain.py:319` `_spawn_detached_drain` | yes | no | `Path.cwd()` in `repo_root` |\n| `_store/push.py:209` async `push_tickets_branch` | yes | no | `git` startup under `run_git` |\n| `_commands/compact_trigger.py:206` `_spawn_detached_sweep` | yes | no | `git` startup under `run_git_write` |\n\nThe other `start_new_session=True` uses in the tree (`grounding/harness.py:176`,\n`jira/acli_subprocess.py:443`, `jira_family/wiki_render.py:384`) are NOT detached — the flag\nis there only so a timeout can `killpg` the group, and the parent blocks on `communicate()`.\nThey are correctly out of scope.\n\n### Defect legitimacy: `defect`\n\nCited contract, in the code's own words: `_spawn_detached_drain` — \"Detach a `rebar enrich\n--drain` child that **outlives the current command**\"; the module docstring — \"DETACHES the\nenrichment to a child that outlives the command\"; `push.py:222` — \"orphan it (own session);\n**survives parent exit**\"; `_spawn_detached_sweep` — \"Detach a sweep child that **outlives\nthis command**\". A child that dies at `getcwd()` the moment its parent's directory is removed\ndoes not satisfy any of those. This is not a feature request or intended behaviour.\n\n### Defect origin: `c1de-d6a0-6cef-4135` (leggy-heedless-mosquito), class `plan_defect`\n\n`git log -L 318,333:src/rebar/llm/enrich_drain.py` gives exactly one commit for the\nimplicated lines: `9ad46965bd` (2026-07-09) \"feat(overlap): Tier-1 opportunistic detached\ndrain + rebar enrich CLI\", trailer `rebar-ticket: c1de-d6a0-6cef-4135`. No carrier to walk\nthrough, and the date test does not fire: there is no good->bad transition, because the site\nwas never right — the `cwd` was omitted in the commit that created the spawn. So this is an\nomission at birth, and here the fix site IS the cause site.\n\n`plan_defect` rather than `regression`: c1de's plan specified the detach down to its exact\nPOSIX flags — \"POSIX reuses push.py's approach (`start_new_session=True`, `close_fds=True`)\n+ its PYTHONPATH bootstrap\" — and simply never considered the child's working directory. A\nreviewer of c1de could plausibly have caught it; that is the escape worth counting.\n\n**Divergence worth recording:** the same plan sentence names `src/rebar/_store/push.py:108`\nas the pattern being copied, and push.py has the same omission — introduced by `57114212cf`\n(2026-06-12, \"feat(tier-d): rebar._store write/sync core\", pre-trailer, no\n`rebar-ticket:`), with `7480964ca0` (a repo-wide `ruff format`) as a pure carrier on top.\n`compact_trigger`'s copy came later still, from `d2dea317ec` (2026-08-13, ticket\n`1fde-becd-942a-4351`), whose docstring says outright that it \"Mirrors\n`enrich_drain._spawn_detached_drain`\". So the omission propagated by deliberate imitation\nacross three tickets. I am still attributing THIS bug to c1de and not to 57114212cf: 5711\ncreated a flawed exemplar, not a contract that c1de was obliged to meet, and the drain's own\ndefect entered the tree with c1de. The two sibling sites are being fixed in scope under this\nticket rather than attributed separately.\n\n### Caller-dependency gate: clear\n\n`_spawn_detached_drain` has exactly one caller (`maybe_drain`), `_spawn_detached_sweep` one,\nand push's spawn is inline in its own async branch. Nothing depends on the child INHERITING\nthe caller's directory: the drain child re-resolves config (and the store root is the correct\nresolution target, reached through the same symlinked tracker), and the push/sweep children\naddress git explicitly with `git -C <path>` and need a live cwd only for git's own startup.\nThe existing tests at all three sites stub the spawn helpers, so none pins the absent kwarg.\nOnly-incidental usage — proceeding to Phase 2."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787266995505379001,"uuid":"1785d86d-b092-40af-a925-e420f9b9756f"}